WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.596
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:11.866 --> 00:14.702
Looks like you did it again. I knew you'd do a good job.

3
00:17.789 --> 00:19.707
You look like you didn't get much sleep.

4
00:22.418 --> 00:24.796
Makes sense. It's not exactly surprising.

5
00:27.382 --> 00:30.009
6,018,000 won.

6
00:31.136 --> 00:32.554
You really went through it.

7
00:33.054 --> 00:35.765
- I wanna stop right now. - Oh, really?

8
00:36.599 --> 00:39.060
The next one's multiplied by 200.

9
00:41.604 --> 00:44.566
I saw people die with my own eyes last night. I'm freaked out.

10
00:44.649 --> 00:49.654
Think about it. If that really happened, the world would be in chaos right now.

11
00:52.907 --> 00:54.450
Are you saying that wasn't real?

12
00:58.037 --> 01:01.749
Hyeok-jun, I believe you're cut out for this.

13
01:02.417 --> 01:04.335
I think it's the right line of work for you.

14
01:04.419 --> 01:06.713
You think I'm some kind of psycho, or what?

15
01:07.881 --> 01:11.759
"Cut out for this?" These crazy-ass jobs are not the right line of work for me.

16
01:14.179 --> 01:15.388
This work,

17
01:16.514 --> 01:18.808
it's work that someone has to be doing.

18
01:21.019 --> 01:25.023
What's most important to you? Think about your real top priority.

19
01:27.483 --> 01:29.152
And think about it carefully now.

20
01:31.529 --> 01:33.907
The answer is probably closer than you think.

21
01:39.454 --> 01:41.122
See you again soon.

22
01:55.595 --> 01:57.639
REST YOUR WEARY BODY WE WILL REMEMBER YOU

23
01:58.223 --> 02:01.935
MAY DELIVERY WORKER KIM CHANG-GYU REST IN PEACE

24
02:21.621 --> 02:22.789
- What's this? - Oh!

25
02:23.373 --> 02:24.999
Does it hit close to home?

26
02:25.500 --> 02:26.584
Uh, hey!

27
02:27.001 --> 02:28.378
Why are you here right now?

28
02:28.461 --> 02:30.880
What the hell is going on? Are you following me?

29
02:30.964 --> 02:31.881
What?

30
02:32.757 --> 02:35.009
You're the one that walked over. I was just standing here.

31
02:35.802 --> 02:36.761
Uh… Uh…

32
02:38.429 --> 02:39.597
Were you out shopping?

33
02:39.681 --> 02:41.391
Uh, sorry, I guess I was lost in my head.

34
02:41.474 --> 02:43.101
You must want to know, right?

35
02:44.102 --> 02:46.396
About Spider Staffing Agency?

36
02:47.355 --> 02:48.398
What are you saying?

37
02:49.607 --> 02:52.902
Aren't you curious if it's all real? Or just an illusion?

38
02:54.279 --> 02:55.863
How does that tea sound now?

39
03:01.869 --> 03:05.039
I'm an accident investigator from the Workers' Compensation Service.

40
03:05.123 --> 03:06.582
You've never heard of that, have you?

41
03:06.666 --> 03:09.168
WORKERS' COMPENSATION SERVICE EUM YEON-JOO, ACCIDENT INVESTIGATOR

42
03:09.252 --> 03:11.296
What does an accident investigator do?

43
03:11.379 --> 03:14.173
There are a lot of agencies with different specialties,

44
03:15.091 --> 03:16.634
and mine focuses on cases

45
03:16.718 --> 03:19.304
that don't quite warrant going to the police.

46
03:19.387 --> 03:22.265
The kind of cases that also wouldn't be suited for civil court.

47
03:22.765 --> 03:24.976
It's where strange cases like that usually end up.

48
03:25.059 --> 03:26.978
What do you mean by "strange cases like that?"

49
03:27.061 --> 03:28.980
What about them is so strange?

50
03:29.063 --> 03:31.107
Hm… For instance,

51
03:32.608 --> 03:34.527
an agency that lures people in

52
03:34.610 --> 03:37.196
with high-paying temp jobs that seem too good to be true.

53
03:37.280 --> 03:38.281
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

54
03:38.364 --> 03:41.326
Then strangely, the workers who show up for those gigs,

55
03:41.826 --> 03:44.746
they always return suffering serious issues.

56
03:44.829 --> 03:47.081
Sometimes, they don't even return at all.

57
03:48.416 --> 03:50.251
Do you have anything to say about that?

58
03:53.713 --> 03:56.466
I can only help you if you tell me what you know.

59
04:16.110 --> 04:16.986
MAJOR FIRE BREAKS OUT

60
04:17.070 --> 04:20.114
"A fire at a university hospital retreat. Multiple deaths."

61
04:20.198 --> 04:21.699
CAUSE UNKNOWN CASUALTIES UNQUANTIFIABLE

62
04:21.783 --> 04:23.451
What I saw, it wasn't this.

63
04:23.534 --> 04:25.828
This wasn't just an accident, I'm sure of it.

64
04:26.537 --> 04:29.207
I tried to believe it was just a hallucination, but I think this was--

65
04:29.290 --> 04:31.793
Being able to make someone see hallucinations

66
04:32.960 --> 04:34.504
as vivid as that one,

67
04:35.088 --> 04:37.006
do you think that's easy to do?

68
04:39.675 --> 04:42.887
I'm glad you're here. And grateful that you're so brave.

69
04:43.846 --> 04:44.806
Uh…

70
04:44.889 --> 04:46.516
I'll be seeing you again, right?

71
04:51.979 --> 04:53.606
I'm not temping anymore.

72
05:53.374 --> 05:56.419
DEAD-END JOB

73
05:57.795 --> 06:00.715
MILKMAN VLOG

74
06:01.674 --> 06:03.634
You really did make some cash.

75
06:03.718 --> 06:06.345
I can't believe you, of all people, took me shopping.

76
06:06.429 --> 06:07.972
I hear when people act super different,

77
06:08.055 --> 06:10.099
it's usually because they're dying or whatever.

78
06:11.392 --> 06:12.894
Odd way to say "thanks."

79
06:12.977 --> 06:15.730
I mean, these new shoes do kinda hurt my feet.

80
06:17.523 --> 06:20.234
If you flub the interview, you'll be in for even more hurt.

81
06:21.235 --> 06:22.570
I gotta head out.

82
06:23.446 --> 06:24.614
Hey, hold on a minute.

83
06:25.114 --> 06:26.532
Oh God, what now?

84
06:33.915 --> 06:34.749
For me?

85
06:48.387 --> 06:50.014
It's not a fake or anything.

86
06:50.515 --> 06:53.226
I bought it on a resale app, but it's real.

87
06:53.309 --> 06:54.352
Why'd you get it?

88
06:56.771 --> 06:59.565
I thought if you had something expensive on you…

89
07:01.526 --> 07:04.028
maybe you'd think you were worth protecting too.

90
07:07.281 --> 07:08.783
I saw that your pull-up bar fell down.

91
07:09.825 --> 07:11.619
And a rope was in the trash.

92
07:14.747 --> 07:16.582
Just don't do anything stupid.

93
07:18.000 --> 07:20.169
- Ji-yoon, if you just-- - I'm gonna go.

94
07:41.232 --> 07:45.111
VERY GOOD EMPLOYMENT AGENCY

95
07:45.194 --> 07:48.072
Everyone in Logistics 1, get on the bus!

96
07:50.199 --> 07:51.242
Logistics 1!

97
07:53.035 --> 07:56.414
Pack the boxes quickly. We need efficiency. Move faster. Come on!

98
07:56.914 --> 08:00.418
Space them out. Sort quickly. Push them forward, then grab more.

99
08:01.544 --> 08:04.839
Scan the barcodes faster! Move it. Come on. Hurry up! Go!

100
08:09.885 --> 08:12.388
God, this is so exhausting.

101
08:21.856 --> 08:24.066
Hey there. Do you think I could get a sip of that?

102
08:25.318 --> 08:26.527
What?

103
08:26.611 --> 08:27.903
You used to say it was okay

104
08:27.987 --> 08:30.573
because we were in the same classroom, Byeon Hyeok-jun.

105
08:30.656 --> 08:32.950
- Are you Kwak Byeong-cheol? - Yeah, man.

106
08:34.702 --> 08:37.997
W… What are you doing here? Your family was so well-off, weren't they?

107
08:38.080 --> 08:40.875
I remember I used to eat at your family's place all the time.

108
08:42.293 --> 08:45.504
Actually, kind of. You're half right.

109
08:46.339 --> 08:49.216
Hey, I was watching you from across the floor just now.

110
08:49.300 --> 08:50.801
You were working your ass off.

111
08:51.302 --> 08:53.554
Of course. I have to work really fucking hard.

112
08:53.638 --> 08:56.432
I might need to spend my whole paycheck on pain patches.

113
08:56.932 --> 08:59.769
It's just because you're new. You'll get used to it if you hang in there.

114
09:03.939 --> 09:06.651
What else can we do if there's no other work for us, right?

115
09:10.655 --> 09:12.531
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY BOSS

116
09:13.407 --> 09:16.077
Seems like you must still be thinking about it.

117
09:16.827 --> 09:19.830
You're gonna miss out on a job that pays 200 times more?

118
09:19.914 --> 09:21.999
So much.

119
09:24.960 --> 09:25.795
What's that?

120
09:27.505 --> 09:28.631
W… What? Um, nothing!

121
09:29.131 --> 09:30.383
Debt collector?

122
09:30.925 --> 09:34.220
Hey! You taking an endless break, Byeong-cheol?

123
09:34.303 --> 09:35.680
Be there in a second!

124
09:36.889 --> 09:39.767
That bastard picks on me all the time. Later.

125
09:40.393 --> 09:41.394
See you later.

126
09:42.269 --> 09:46.273
Hey, by the way, careful. Don't overwork yourself too much.

127
09:46.357 --> 09:47.733
You might not be able to call out.

128
09:47.817 --> 09:50.236
Last week, someone had a heart attack and they still made him--

129
09:50.319 --> 09:52.113
- You better hurry your ass up! - Bye.

130
09:53.572 --> 09:55.950
Wow. How did he get here?

131
10:10.047 --> 10:12.216
STILL THINKING ABOUT IT? WILL YOU MISS A 200X-PAYING GIG?

132
10:12.299 --> 10:14.927
I can't do it. Just forget it.

133
10:18.347 --> 10:19.557
DELETE ALL

134
10:31.152 --> 10:32.361
Mm.

135
10:34.155 --> 10:37.408
Hello, this is the HR team at Xenon calling for Byeon Hyeok-jun.

136
10:37.491 --> 10:40.828
We're reaching out to let you know that you passed our document screening process.

137
10:40.911 --> 10:42.121
Me? Really?

138
10:42.204 --> 10:43.789
Yes. I'll send you an address.

139
10:43.873 --> 10:46.584
Can you come in for an interview at 4 p.m. today?

140
10:48.919 --> 10:50.004
Whoa.

141
10:58.053 --> 10:59.805
INTERVIEWEES THIS WAY

142
11:09.774 --> 11:11.734
Ms. Kim Si-yeon, is there a Kim Si-yeon here?

143
11:11.817 --> 11:14.236
- Yes. - Right over here.

144
11:17.406 --> 11:19.575
- Mr. Moon Jae-eun? - Yes, I'm here!

145
11:19.658 --> 11:21.619
"High-earning multi-level tech jobs?"

146
11:24.538 --> 11:27.041
You'll be a great fit. I know you'll be raking it in.

147
11:28.334 --> 11:30.628
Goddamn it. I should have fucking known.

148
11:34.465 --> 11:36.091
Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun!

149
11:40.054 --> 11:42.723
Byeon Hyeok-jun, your interview is up next.

150
11:46.435 --> 11:48.229
Is Byeon Hyeok-jun not here?

151
11:51.565 --> 11:52.900
Oh, that must be you.

152
11:52.983 --> 11:54.819
Here, just put this on first.

153
11:55.486 --> 11:57.947
RÉSUMÉ BYEON HYEOK-JUN

154
11:58.030 --> 11:59.281
No, thanks.

155
12:01.033 --> 12:03.536
Yeah, that's how you end up living on the street.

156
12:06.330 --> 12:08.082
Han? Han Do-yeon?

157
12:08.749 --> 12:10.543
Is Han Do-yeon here?

158
12:12.086 --> 12:13.003
Is there…

159
12:16.298 --> 12:17.132
What?

160
12:18.050 --> 12:19.051
You know what?

161
12:20.719 --> 12:23.597
I was going to visit my mom, who I barely see, but I came here.

162
12:24.557 --> 12:27.476
I transferred buses twice and skipped lunch to get here, but this…

163
12:28.936 --> 12:30.646
- This is a pyramid scheme, isn't it? - Wait.

164
12:30.729 --> 12:34.024
- It's a high-earning, multi-level big-- - Yes, it is. Yes it is!

165
12:38.195 --> 12:40.447
No, it isn't. Of course not!

166
12:40.990 --> 12:44.159
That guy obviously has no idea what he's talking about.

167
12:53.460 --> 12:54.545
How's it going?

168
12:54.628 --> 12:56.547
Oh, hey, Hyeok-jun.

169
12:57.047 --> 13:00.634
Do you get off work soon? Let's get pork belly or something.

170
13:00.718 --> 13:03.178
Oh, man, pork belly sounds so good right now,

171
13:03.262 --> 13:05.222
but this isn't really the time.

172
13:14.106 --> 13:16.191
Hey, man, what happened to you?

173
13:16.692 --> 13:19.028
It's rhabdomyolysis, apparently.

174
13:19.528 --> 13:21.155
Something like that.

175
13:22.489 --> 13:24.491
I didn't think work would give me any time off.

176
13:27.036 --> 13:30.039
- When do you get discharged? - I don't even know.

177
13:30.122 --> 13:32.207
They're observing a few days.

178
13:33.000 --> 13:36.003
If nothing changes, I could need kidney dialysis.

179
13:47.848 --> 13:50.726
RE: WORK INJURY CLAIM

180
13:50.809 --> 13:53.854
"The company bears no responsibility whatsoever?"

181
13:54.980 --> 13:57.441
Seriously? Those fucking assholes.

182
13:58.692 --> 14:01.403
The company won't pay my hospital bills?

183
14:02.571 --> 14:05.991
Man, I don't even have private insurance. Am I supposed to just die?

184
14:12.456 --> 14:13.332
Hm?

185
14:14.959 --> 14:17.544
Hey, Mr. Hyeok-jun.

186
14:18.379 --> 14:21.590
How's it going? Have you found another gig yet?

187
14:21.674 --> 14:23.050
In the standard pay range?

188
14:23.133 --> 14:24.718
I need money soon.

189
14:24.802 --> 14:27.304
That job you mentioned that pays 200 times more? Is it--

190
14:33.268 --> 14:36.105
HEUKRAN OFFICETEL, MILKMAN 200 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 10 P.M. - 6 A.M.

191
14:38.983 --> 14:42.486
They just want me to do a… milk delivery?

192
14:42.569 --> 14:44.279
Yes, it's a milk delivery.

193
14:44.363 --> 14:46.365
The wage is calculated for an eight-hour day,

194
14:46.448 --> 14:49.660
but you could easily finish the gig in about an hour, I'd assume.

195
14:50.703 --> 14:53.122
I bet you could never find a gig as easy as that.

196
14:54.123 --> 14:57.960
And that should be more than enough to cover your friend's hospital bills.

197
15:29.783 --> 15:30.617
Okay.

198
15:59.646 --> 16:02.107
I bet you could never find a gig as easy as that.

199
16:02.191 --> 16:03.484
Well, I hope so.

200
16:11.033 --> 16:11.992
YEONGSAN MILK

201
16:16.997 --> 16:18.248
Eleven bottles.

202
16:18.749 --> 16:20.000
You've got this.

203
16:21.043 --> 16:23.295
HEUKRAN OFFICETEL MILKMAN 200 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE

204
16:23.378 --> 16:24.797
STARTS AT 10 P.M. ENDS AT 6 A.M.

205
16:28.258 --> 16:30.511
- Here for a delivery? - Whoa! You scared me.

206
16:31.637 --> 16:33.889
Sorry, what did you ask? A delivery, yeah.

207
16:33.972 --> 16:36.141
Mm!

208
16:38.310 --> 16:39.645
You won't skip any, right?

209
16:42.397 --> 16:43.857
I'll get it all, yeah.

210
16:43.941 --> 16:45.609
Finish in under an hour,

211
16:45.692 --> 16:47.986
or you might not be able to leave this place.

212
16:49.279 --> 16:51.949
What do you mean by "this place"? I mean, not being able to leave?

213
16:52.032 --> 16:54.201
Just do it all in an hour.

214
16:56.829 --> 16:57.830
Uh, sure.

215
17:00.499 --> 17:01.500
Hold on.

216
17:05.587 --> 17:06.880
What's that in your bag?

217
17:07.464 --> 17:08.298
What?

218
17:10.509 --> 17:12.136
Oh, uh…

219
17:12.219 --> 17:15.097
Oh, this stuff? It's really nothing. It's, uh…

220
17:17.599 --> 17:19.268
What is all of this?

221
17:20.686 --> 17:22.354
You gonna rob us or what?

222
17:23.564 --> 17:25.315
N… No, of course not.

223
17:26.608 --> 17:27.985
Get them on your way out.

224
17:36.577 --> 17:38.829
You have one hour. Just one.

225
17:44.251 --> 17:46.461
Just don't make any delivery errors, all right?

226
17:46.545 --> 17:48.630
It won't be easy, though.

227
17:53.802 --> 17:56.430
Ah, sh…

228
18:02.394 --> 18:04.897
Uh, this is just in case, um…

229
18:05.439 --> 18:08.734
If something messed up happens while I do the deliveries…

230
18:08.817 --> 18:10.277
What the fuck am I even saying?

231
18:13.155 --> 18:14.489
Uh, this is Hyeok-jun.

232
18:15.073 --> 18:18.368
I'm filming a milk delivery thing.

233
18:19.661 --> 18:22.080
Six bottles to the second floor, four to the fourth floor,

234
18:22.164 --> 18:23.290
one to the fifth floor.

235
18:23.373 --> 18:25.417
Sounds good, I'll start the delivery.

236
18:43.852 --> 18:45.187
As fast as I can.

237
18:45.270 --> 18:47.773
232, 223.

238
18:49.191 --> 18:50.734
One for 215.

239
18:51.693 --> 18:52.778
This one's unit 210.

240
18:53.362 --> 18:54.529
Okay, 206.

241
18:55.030 --> 18:57.324
And then the next one is 202.

242
19:01.286 --> 19:02.829
Where the hell is 202?

243
19:04.498 --> 19:06.124
That one's 204.

244
19:06.625 --> 19:08.252
That's 203.

245
19:08.335 --> 19:09.419
201.

246
19:09.503 --> 19:12.381
What? Shouldn't it be here?

247
19:16.635 --> 19:19.096
232, 233…

248
19:26.603 --> 19:28.063
What the hell is going on?

249
19:30.482 --> 19:31.525
Ah, sh…

250
19:32.025 --> 19:34.444
I don't have time. I'll just do the other floors first.

251
19:41.994 --> 19:43.328
Is anyone there?

252
19:52.713 --> 19:54.298
Wait, what's going on here?

253
19:55.090 --> 19:56.800
What is this shit?

254
19:59.136 --> 20:01.471
I just need to do this. Let's go.

255
20:13.984 --> 20:14.818
Ah, sh…

256
20:30.292 --> 20:31.209
Oh…

257
20:31.877 --> 20:34.546
The fourth floor only needs one delivery. I'll go there first.

258
20:38.550 --> 20:39.926
Oh, shit!

259
20:43.263 --> 20:45.682
Why are they all 444?

260
20:50.854 --> 20:51.772
No way.

261
20:57.861 --> 21:00.280
All these fours are such a bad sign. Oh!

262
21:05.619 --> 21:07.496
Is it this one? How do I…

263
21:09.247 --> 21:11.875
Why does every single apartment have the same number?

264
21:15.504 --> 21:18.382
Four divided by four… plus four?

265
21:23.595 --> 21:25.764
Are they messing with me? This is crazy.

266
21:27.933 --> 21:29.267
444.

267
21:36.942 --> 21:37.776
Let's go.

268
21:44.324 --> 21:45.367
Wait, what?

269
21:46.576 --> 21:47.994
What's going on here?

270
21:50.997 --> 21:53.208
Just don't make any delivery errors, all right?

271
21:54.209 --> 21:55.210
Errors.

272
21:58.255 --> 21:59.548
It's in the right place.

273
22:01.091 --> 22:02.092
Huh?

274
22:06.847 --> 22:08.390
Oh no! God, no!

275
22:08.473 --> 22:10.934
What's wrong with the timer? How much time do I have?

276
22:16.898 --> 22:17.941
Not this one.

277
22:18.024 --> 22:18.984
Or this one.

278
22:19.067 --> 22:20.235
Nope.

279
22:20.318 --> 22:21.903
Shit. What the fuck is going on?

280
22:21.987 --> 22:23.363
It's this one!

281
22:33.123 --> 22:34.416
I can still do this.

282
22:34.499 --> 22:36.293
515, fifth floor first.

283
22:36.376 --> 22:37.294
Okay.

284
22:38.962 --> 22:41.173
Fifth floor, let's go.

285
22:42.883 --> 22:44.092
Third floor?

286
22:46.845 --> 22:47.846
It's five, right?

287
22:49.014 --> 22:49.973
What?

288
22:57.189 --> 22:58.482
What the fuck is this? Come on!

289
23:01.693 --> 23:04.905
What the hell is happening? This goddamn building is insane!

290
23:14.331 --> 23:15.582
Ah, sh…

291
23:22.130 --> 23:23.089
Oh my God!

292
23:25.759 --> 23:27.636
Fuck! Seriously?

293
23:47.280 --> 23:48.114
Damn it.

294
23:48.865 --> 23:49.866
Fuck this.

295
23:52.619 --> 23:54.120
Oh. Uh…

296
23:56.581 --> 23:59.793
RESIDENTS ONLY

297
24:06.049 --> 24:07.300
Oh, shit.

298
24:19.938 --> 24:21.231
Where's the door handle?

